  Check SQL migration files for statements that lock tables,
  rewrite them or break running code.

  Pass one or more .sql files, or - to read SQL from
  standard input.

  Usage
    migrail check <file.sql>... | - [flags]

  Flags
        --ci                  CI mode: no color,
                              links or spinners
                              unless forced
        --compact             print one line per finding
        --db-version string   PostgreSQL major
                              version in production,
                              such as 16 (default: 12)
        --fail-on string      exit with code 1 on
                              findings at or above:
                              error, warning, notice
                              or never (default "error")
    -f, --format string       output format: pretty
                              or json (default "pretty")
    -q, --quiet               print only findings
                              and the summary
    -r, --rule strings        only run these rules,
                              by ID or slug
        --skip-rule strings   skip these rules, by
                              ID or slug
    -v, --verbose             print each phase with
                              its timing

  Global flags
        --ascii           use ASCII symbols instead
                          of Unicode
        --color string    use color: auto, always or
                          never (default "auto")
        --no-hyperlinks   don't print clickable file
                          links
        --theme string    color theme: auto, dark,
                          light or mono (default "auto")
